# === PLACEHOLDER (pending Warren key generation by poka) ===========
#
# The pubkey below is the upstream `mullvad-update/test-pubkey` value
# repurposed as a Warren placeholder so the `Vec1<VerifyingKey>`
# LazyLock initialiser has at least one valid key to deserialise. Any
# real Warren update manifest signed by an actual production privkey
# will fail verification under this placeholder, which is the safe-by-
# default outcome until the real key lands here.
#
# To deploy real Warren updates:
#   1. poka generates an Ed25519 keypair offline (privkey kept secret).
#   2. The 32-byte pubkey is encoded to hex and replaces the line below.
#   3. CI release workflow signs every published `latest.json` /
#      `*.json` manifest with the matching privkey.
#   4. A `warren-vpn` daemon shipped with the new pubkey trust file
#      will accept the signed manifest and surface the update banner.
#
# Multiple production keys may be listed once a key-rotation policy is
# defined (mirror upstream Mullvad's 5-developer-key scheme if desired).
